WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.913
Two guards make this gate honest.

2
00:00:01.913 --> 00:00:04.088
First, the organization call.

3
00:00:04.088 --> 00:00:08.888
Google's REST reference documents it, but
the G cloud flags for it weren't read.

4
00:00:08.888 --> 00:00:11.519
So the kit's call list
marks it unverified,

5
00:00:11.519 --> 00:00:16.087
and the live invoker refuses to run
it unless you pass allow unverified.

6
00:00:16.087 --> 00:00:18.525
The kit doesn't run a command on a guess.

7
00:00:18.525 --> 00:00:21.700
That's the guide's interim
path for an organization.

8
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.287
Second, the gaps.

9
00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:25.979
Every project records
that Google's planned

10
00:00:25.979 --> 00:00:28.525
maintenance doesn't come
through this A P I.

11
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:33.979
And any workload in an Assured Workloads
FedRAMP or I L package records that it has

12
00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:39.513
no Personalized Service Health to read;
the ISSO decides the compensating channel.

13
00:00:39.513 --> 00:00:43.646
The guide lists the danger plainly:
Google maintenance assumed covered,

14
00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:46.401
and a maintenance window
lands with nobody told.

15
00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:49.337
The guard is the gap
itself, in the record,

16
00:00:49.337 --> 00:00:53.075
in the digest's provider
table and in the ISSO's file.

17
00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:58.540
Until the A P I carries maintenance, it
reaches the agency by the contacts it sets.
